; EpoCanva P3.1 -- exports of the unregistered TSF text service DLL.
;
; Exactly two exports, because exactly two behaviours exist in this round:
;   DllGetClassObject  the COM class-object entry a host (or the test program, through
;                      GetProcAddress) calls to reach IClassFactory
;   DllCanUnloadNow    the unload verdict driven by platforms/windows/tsf/module_state.h
;
; Both are marked PRIVATE: they are entry points for GetProcAddress and for the COM
; loader, and nothing is ever linked against an import library for this DLL (the
; lifecycle program loads it by absolute path only). PRIVATE keeps them out of any
; import library and is what the linker expects for hand-exported symbols like these
; (LNK4104 otherwise); it does not affect GetProcAddress, which resolves them by name
; from the export table either way.
;
; Deliberately ABSENT: DllRegisterServer and DllUnregisterServer. This round performs no
; registry write, no profile registration and no category registration; an export that
; does not exist cannot be handed to regsvr32 by accident. The lifecycle test asserts
; both names are absent from this export table rather than trusting this comment.
EXPORTS
    DllCanUnloadNow     PRIVATE
    DllGetClassObject   PRIVATE
